---
title: High-to-Low Cable Flyes
type: docs
prev: docs/grud/
---
![сведение рук в кроссовере сверху стоя](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5423b04e-fb2f-4b69-9b2d-739b199c8051)

{{% steps %}}

### Step 1
Attach single handles to the high pulleys on both sides and stand in the center of the cable crossover machine. Lean your torso slightly forward and place one foot forward (or keep a wide stance) for solid balance.

### Step 2
Pull the handles down and together in a wide hugging motion toward your lower chest/hips.

### Step 3
Inhale and slowly open your arms back up to shoulder height (no further), then exhale and sweep them back down in a wide arc, squeezing your chest muscles firmly at the bottom.

{{% /steps %}}

{{< callout type="info" >}}
• Do not press the handles like a chest press—keep a soft, fixed bend in your elbows and move your hands in a wide arc (like hugging a large tree).

• When opening your arms, keep your elbows pointing slightly up and back.

• Keep your core tight and your upper body still throughout the movement.

• Focus entirely on pulling with your chest muscles rather than pushing with your arms.

• Exhale as you bring your hands together, and inhale as you open your arms.
{{< /callout >}}
